# Notion board status

Keep [TeaBot Board](https://www.notion.so/e9ac72418e71476a96bb026e155eb121) in sync. Property `Status` (select), exact values:

`Backlog` | `To Do` | `In Progress` | `Review` | `Done` | `Blocked`

## Взял в разработку → In Progress

Before writing code, search the board and set `Status` = `In Progress`.

Triggers: user picks a card, "давай сделаем X", "возьми задачу", implementing a named board item.

## Выполнил → Done

After the card's acceptance criteria are actually met, set `Status` = `Done`.

Triggers: user says выполнил / готово / done, or you finished the checklist.

## How (Notion MCP)

1. Auth if the Notion namespace needs it (`mcp_auth`).
2. Search/fetch the card on TeaBot Board (do not invent a page).
3. `notion-update-page`: `command=update_properties`, `Status` = `In Progress` or `Done`.
4. Tell the user the card moved.

## Do not

- Use other labels (`Done` not `DONE`; `In Progress` not `In progress`).
- Mark `Done` if tests fail, the user still owes a decision, or work is blocked (`Blocked` instead).
- Leave a started card on `To Do` / `Backlog`.
- Create a duplicate card if search finds none — ask which task to update.
